[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Immurk brings touch style security to any Mac and Linux. A long press on the device sensor instantly locks the screen. One touch on the sensor, no password typed, and we\'re back in.'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The same fingerprint unlocks privileged commands in the terminal. Sudo just asks for a touch. Get pulls over SSH. The first call is'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'already up to date. Run it again and Immurk prompts you to verify your fingerprints. Then signs the SSH challenge right on the device.'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Same flow for raw SSH. Connecting to the pie without typing a passphrase. One touch approves the signature. Beyond a human user, Immurk also gates'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'AI coding agents. We launch Claude code and ask it to authenticate through Immurk. The agent auto loads our ink skills,'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'learning how to ask for authorization. Every privileged command is wrapped with think run the agent. So the agent has to wait for your fingerprints before anything runs.'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'A simple echo is gated by a single fingerprint touch. Sudo and fails. The end flag skips pam,'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'so our pre-auth never applies. But a normal sudo homie goes through cleanly. Fingerprint backed roots.'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Now the real test. Get push triggered an SSH signing request.'

[01:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And the dry run reaches GitHub right after a single touch. Lock, unlock, sudo, SSH, get OTP, all'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'unified behind one touch. Finally, let\'s look at a real-world test case. We open the GitHub sign-in page. The'

[02:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'password is auto-filled for us. When two-factor authentication is required, a Miró OTP picker pops up. Pick the matching entry, fingerprint'

[02:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gated, and the code is typed for you. Verified, signed in. That\'s Miró touch-it style security for everyone.'
